From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Decrypt Blu-ray discs with MakeMKV

A Blu-ray disc in a drive is encrypted, and libaacs opens it only with
that disc's key in a key file the user has to fill. MakeMKV's libmmbd
stands in for libaacs and libbdplus and gets the keys itself; libbluray
takes it when Kodi names it (the makemkv package's kodi.service drop-in).
The makemkv package (overlay) builds MakeMKV's open source part, and
makemkv-bin installs its program as MakeMKV ships it, as its licence
allows a distribution to.

diff --git a/packages/multimedia/libbluray/package.mk b/packages/multimedia/libbluray/package.mk
--- a/packages/multimedia/libbluray/package.mk
+++ b/packages/multimedia/libbluray/package.mk
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ PKG_DEPENDS_TARGET="toolchain fontconfig freetype libxml2 libudfread"
 PKG_LONGDESC="libbluray is an open-source library designed for Blu-Ray Discs playback for media players."
 
 if [ "${BLURAY_AACS_SUPPORT}" = "yes" ]; then
-  PKG_DEPENDS_TARGET+=" libaacs"
+  PKG_DEPENDS_TARGET+=" libaacs makemkv"
 fi
 
 if [ "${BLURAY_BDPLUS_SUPPORT}" = "yes" ]; then
